Founder of the Church of the Resurrection and pastor [[Adam Hamilton (pastor)|Adam Hamilton]],<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kelly |first1=Matthew |last2=Bayless |first2=Kacen |title=Popular KC-area pastor launches challenge to Roger Marshall - with a twist |url=https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article315578310.html |website=The Star |publisher=McClatchy Media |access-date=April 30, 2026}}</ref> who initially considered running as an independent,<ref>{{cite news |last2=Bayless |first2=Kacen |last1=Kelly |first1=Matthew |title=Popular KC-area pastor considers independent Senate run to unseat Roger Marshall |url=https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article314837324.html |access-date=February 27, 2026 |work=[[Kansas City Star]] |date=February 27, 2026}}</ref> won the Democratic nomination with 35% of the vote. He defeated a field that included former state [[USDA]] Director Christy Davis,<ref name="DavisKS">{{cite news |last1=Newton |first1=Ryan |title=Kansas Democrat launches campaign for US Senate against incumbent Roger Marshall |url=https://www.ksn.com/news/your-local-election-hq/kansas-democrat-launches-campaign-for-us-senate-against-incumbent-roger-marshall/ |access-date=August 21, 2025 |publisher=[[KSNW]] |date=August 19, 2025}}</ref> former federal prosecutor Jason Hart,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Alatidd |first1=Jason |title=Kansas prosecutor Jason Hart joins Senate race, eyes Trump and Marshall |url=https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/congressional/2026/03/11/former-federal-prosecutor-joins-senate-primary-to-face-roger-marshall/89066799007/ |access-date=March 17, 2026 |work=Topeka Capital-Journal |date=March 11, 2026}}</ref> commercial real estate developer Erik Murray,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Cooper |first1=Brad |title=KCK developer announces for U.S. Senate as Democratic primary grows to five |url=https://sunflowerstatejournal.com/kck-developer-announces-for-u-s-senate-as-democratic-primary-grows-to-five/ |access-date=December 3, 2025 |work=Sunflower State Journal |date=December 3, 2025}}</ref> attorney Anne Parelkar,<ref name="Parelkar" /> [[Kansas Senate|state senator]] [[Patrick Schmidt (politician)|Patrick Schmidt]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Alatidd|first1=Jason |title=Topeka Democrat joins US Senate primary to challenge Roger Marshall |url=https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/congressional/2026/02/04/topeka-democrat-patrick-schmidt-joins-senate-race-vs-roger-marshall/88507396007/ |access-date=February 4, 2026 |work=The Topeka Capital-Journal |date=February 4, 2026}}</ref> art gallery owner Mike Soetaertare,<ref name="Parelkar">{{cite news |last1=Kaminski |first1=Anna |title=Democratic immigration lawyer wants to fix broken system with run for U.S. Senate in Kansas |url=https://kansasreflector.com/2025/08/25/democratic-immigration-lawyer-wants-to-fix-broken-system-with-run-for-u-s-senate-in-kansas/ |access-date=August 27, 2025 |work=Kansas Reflector |date=August 25, 2025}}</ref> former financial services executive Sandy Spidel Neumann,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Cooper |first1=Brad |title=Democrat launches bid for U.S. Senate, expands party primary to four |url=https://sunflowerstatejournal.com/democrat-launches-bid-for-u-s-senate-expands-party-primary-to-four/ |access-date=October 16, 2025 |work=Sunflower State Journal |date=October 16, 2025}}</ref> and counterintelligence specialist Noah Tyler.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Saldanha-Olson |first1=Stacey |title=Afghanistan veteran Noah Taylor enters U.S. Senate race for Kansas |url=https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/state/2026/03/17/afghanistan-veteran-noah-taylor-runs-for-u-s-senate-from-kansas/89184140007/ |access-date=March 17, 2026 |work=[[The Topeka Capital-Journal]] |date=March 17, 2026}}</ref>
