{{Main|2026 United States Senate election in Maine}}
{{See also|List of United States senators from Maine}}
Incumbent Republican Senator [[Susan Collins]] was reelected with 51% of the vote to 42% for her Democratic opponent in [[2020 United States Senate election in Maine|2020]]. She formally announced her reelection campaign in February 2026.<ref name="Collins">{{Cite web |last=Collins |first=Susan |date=February 10, 2026 |title=Susan Collins: I'm running for reelection because experience and independence matter for Maine |url=https://www.bangordailynews.com/2026/02/10/opinion/opinion-contributor/susan-collins-reelection-experience-independence-matter/ |access-date=February 10, 2026 |website=Bangor Daily News |language=en-US}}</ref> As the only person to submit the necessary number of signatures to appear on the primary ballot, Collins is the Republican nominee.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Reed |first=Russ |date=March 16, 2026 |title=Here's who qualified to appear on Maine 2026 primary ballot |url=https://www.wmtw.com/article/maine-candidates-on-2026-primary-ballot/70763044 |access-date=March 17, 2026 |publisher=WMTW |language=en}}</ref>

According to [[Federal Election Commission]] (FEC) records, as of October 2026, Collins has received $4,525,846 from [[Political action committee|political action committees]] (PACs) affiliated with pro-Israel lobbies; of this amount, $3,670,038 is attributed to the 2026 election cycle.<ref>{{Cite web |title= Does Susan Collins Take AIPAC Money? FEC Filings (2026) — AIPAC Tracker |url= https://whofundsmyrep.com/rep/susan-m-collins |access-date= 2026-10-19 |website= WhoFundsMyRep |language=en}}</ref>

Throughout 2025, [[Governor of Maine|Governor]] [[Janet Mills]] was seen as a potential Democratic challenger to Collins. She announced her Senate candidacy in October,<ref name="MillsME">{{Cite web |last2=Whittle |first2=Patrick |last1=Beaumont |first1=Thomas |date=October 14, 2025 |title=Maine Gov. Mills plans to confront President Trump again with her campaign for the US Senate |url=https://apnews.com/article/maine-mills-senate-trump-collins-e669e25547d5343cee5c3431e14e09b4 |access-date=October 14, 2025 |publisher=[[Associated Press]] |language=en}}</ref> and pledged to serve only one term if elected.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pindell |first=James |date=October 14, 2025 |title=Maine Governor Janet Mills launches Senate bid, stressing electability and pledge to serve only one term |url=https://www.bostonglobe.com/2025/10/14/nation/janet-mills-susan-collins-senate/ |access-date=October 14, 2025 |website=The Boston Globe |language=en-US}}</ref> She suspended her campaign on April 30, 2026, due to a lack of financial resources and poor polling numbers.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lerer |first1=Lisa |last2=Glueck |first2=Katie |last3=Epstein |first3=Reid J. |title=Janet Mills, Governor of Maine, Suspends Senate Campaign |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/30/us/politics/janet-mills-drops-out-senate-race-platner-schumer.html |access-date=April 30, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=April 30, 2026}}</ref> 

On June 9, [[Sullivan, Maine|Sullivan]] [[harbor master]] and [[United States Marine Corps|Marine]] veteran [[Graham Platner]]<ref name="Platner">{{cite news |last1=Otterbein |first1=Holly |title=Maine oyster farmer wants to upend Democratic politics with Senate bid |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2025/08/19/graham-platner-maine-senate-campaign-launch-00513884 |access-date=August 19, 2025 |work=[[Politico]] |date=August 19, 2025}}</ref> defeated former deputy secretary of the [[Maryland Department of the Environment]] David Costello<ref name="CostelloME">{{cite news |last1=Billings |first1=Randy |title=Brunswick Democrat announces campaign for Susan Collins' Senate seat |url=https://www.pressherald.com/2025/06/11/brunswick-democrat-announces-campaign-for-susan-collins-senate-seat/ |access-date=June 11, 2025 |work=[[Portland Press Herald]] |date=June 11, 2025}}</ref> for the Democratic nomination with 72% of the vote.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bradner |first=Eric |date=June 10, 2026 |title=Graham Platner tears into Republicans after clinching Susan Collins matchup in Maine, and other primary night takeaways |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/06/09/politics/graham-platner-susan-collins-maine-south-carolina-primary-election-takeaways |access-date=June 10, 2026 |publisher=CNN |language=en}}</ref>

On July 8, Platner announced his withdrawal from the race, following allegations of sexual assault, which he denied. The same day, Maine Democrats voted to hold a state convention to select a replacement nominee.<ref>{{cite news |title=Live updates: Graham Platner suspends Senate bid as Maine Democrats vie to replace him |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/live-blog/graham-platner-maine-senate-election-trump-live-updates-rcna353556 |access-date=July 8, 2026 |work=[[NBC]] |date=July 8, 2026}}</ref> Candidates seeking the nomination were required to collect at least 500 signatures, including 50 from each of eight counties.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mistler |first=Steve |date=July 10, 2026 |title=The latest on how Maine Democrats will nominate Graham Platner's replacement |url=https://www.mainepublic.org/politics/2026-07-10/the-latest-on-how-maine-democrats-will-nominate-graham-platners-replacement |access-date=July 10, 2026 |website=[[Maine Public]] |language=en}}</ref> During county meetings to select convention delegates, approximately 456 delegates pledged their support to former state Senator [[Troy Jackson]].<ref name="BangorDelegateResults">{{Cite news |last=Shepherd |first=Michael |date=July 13, 2026 |title=Troy Jackson closes in on Maine's Democratic Senate nod after dominant caucus day |url=https://www.bangordailynews.com/2026/07/18/politics/elections/troy-jackson-dominates-day-1-maine-democratic-senate-caucus/ |work=[[Bangor Daily News]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 19, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Svitek |first1=Patrick |last2=Cohen |first2=Ethan |date=July 18, 2026 |title=Troy Jackson, a former Graham Platner ally, well-positioned to win Maine Democrats' nomination to face Sen. Susan Collins |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/18/politics/troy-jackson-graham-platner-maine |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 18, 2026}}</ref><ref name="Pellish & Howard 2026">{{cite news |last1=Pellish |first1=Aaron |last2=Howard |first2=Andrew |date=July 19, 2026 |title=Troy Jackson has effectively secured the Maine Senate Democratic nomination |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2026/07/19/troy-jackson-likely-maine-senate-nominee-platner-01004490 |website=Politico |language=en-US |access-date=July 19, 2026}}</ref> Jackson subsequently defeated Saundra Pelletier at the convention by a vote of 566–5.<ref name="ConvResultUsaToday">{{Cite news |last1=Condon |first1=Emily R. |last2=Margie |first2=Cullen |title=Troy Jackson replaces Graham Platner as Maine Senate Democratic nominee |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2026/07/25/troy-jackson-replaces-graham-platner-maine-senate-democrat-nominee/91020463007/ |work=[[USA Today]] |date=July 25, 2026 |access-date=July 25, 2026}}</ref>
