One-term Republican [[Cindy Hyde-Smith]] was [[2020 United States Senate election in Mississippi|reelected in 2020]] with 54.1% of the vote after being appointed in 2018 and winning a [[2018 United States Senate special election in Mississippi|special election]] later that year. She is running for a second full term in office.<ref name="HydeSmith">{{cite news |last1=Mitchell |first1=J. T. |title=Sen. Cindy Hyde-Smith announces she will seek reelection in 2026 |url=https://www.supertalk.fm/sen-cindy-hyde-smith-announces-she-will-seek-reelection-in-2026/ |access-date=March 7, 2024 |work=[[Supertalk Mississippi]] |date=March 7, 2024}}</ref> She defeated [[Medical doctor|physician]] Sarah Adlakha in the Republican primary on March 10, 2026.<ref name="Adlakha">{{cite news |last1=Corder |first1=Frank |title=Hyde-Smith draws GOP challenger as Democrats target her Mississippi U.S. Senate seat |url=https://magnoliatribune.com/2025/05/09/hyde-smith-draws-gop-challenger-as-democrats-target-her-mississippi-u-s-senate-seat/ |access-date=May 9, 2025 |work=Magnolia Tribune |date=May 9, 2025}}</ref>

[[Lowndes County, Mississippi|Lowndes County]] [[District Attorney]] [[Scott Colom]] defeated [[U.S. Marine Corps]] veteran Albert Littell, and Priscilla Williams-Till, a cousin of [[Emmett Till]], in the Democratic primary on March 10, 2026.<ref name="Colom">{{cite news |last1=McRae |first1=Emma |title=Colom announces Senate run for Hyde-Smith's seat |url=https://cdispatch.com/news/colom-announces-senate-run-for-hyde-smiths-seat/ |access-date=September 3, 2025 |work=[[The Commercial Dispatch]] |date=September 3, 2025}}</ref><ref name="WilliamsTill">{{cite news |last1=Harrison |first1=Heather |title=Emmett Till's Cousin Is Running for US Senate in Mississippi |url=https://www.mississippifreepress.org/priscilla-williams-till-emmett-tills-cousin-is-running-for-us-senate-in-mississippi/ |access-date=September 9, 2025 |work=Mississippi Free Press |date=September 9, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Meet the US Senate candidates in Mississippi 2026 primary election|url=https://www.clarionledger.com/story/news/politics/elections/2026/02/27/united-states-senate-candidates-election-2026-in-mississippi/88839755007/|access-date=February 27, 2026|website=Clarion Ledger}}</ref>

Ty Pinkins, the Democratic nominee for [[Secretary of State of Mississippi|Secretary of State]] in [[2023 Mississippi elections#Secretary of state|2023]] and for [[United States Senate|U.S. Senate]] in [[2024 United States Senate election in Mississippi|2024]], is running as an independent.<ref name="Pinkins">{{cite news |last1=McLaughlin |first1=Grant |title=Pinkins leaving MS Democratic Party, running as independent. What to know |url=https://www.clarionledger.com/story/news/politics/2025/07/01/ty-pinkins-leaving-mississippi-democratic-party/84427842007/ |access-date=July 1, 2025 |work=The Clarion-Ledger |date=July 1, 2025}}</ref>
