Two-term Republican [[Steve Daines]] was [[2020 United States Senate election in Montana|reelected in 2020]] with 55% of the vote. On March 4, 2026, Daines announced he would not seek reelection. The same day, [[United States Attorney|U.S. Attorney]] [[Kurt Alme]] announced his candidacy and immediately won Daines's endorsement.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Szpaller |first=Keila |date=March 5, 2026 |title=Kurt Alme files for U.S. Senate, immediately endorsed by outgoing Sen. Daines, President Trump |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/kurt-alme-files-u-senate-024946223.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260305190705/https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/kurt-alme-files-u-senate-024946223.html |archive-date=March 5, 2026 |access-date=March 15, 2026 |website=Yahoo News |language=en-US}}</ref>

Former [[Montana House of Representatives|state Representative]] [[Reilly Neill]] ran for the Democratic nomination,<ref name="Neill">{{cite web |title=Park County resident runs for U.S. Senate |url=https://www.livingstonenterprise.com/news/park-county-resident-runs-for-u-s-senate/article_ab8f7c38-a65f-11ef-be7b-4fff72cbb547.html |website=[[The Livingston Enterprise]] |date=November 19, 2024 |access-date=November 23, 2024}}</ref> but was defeated in the Democratic primary by former [[U.S. Air Force]] [[Lieutenant Colonel]] Alani Bankhead in a major [[Upset (competition)|upset]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/5897882-live-results-montana-senate-primaries/ |title=Live results: Montana Senate primaries |website=The Hill}}</ref>

[[Seth Bodnar]], the president of the [[University of Montana]] until January 2026, is running as an independent candidate.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ambarian|first1=Jonathon|title=Bodnar announces independent run for Senate|url=https://www.kxlh.com/news/bodnar-announces-independent-run-for-senate|access-date=March 4, 2026|publisher=[[KXLH]]|date=March 4, 2026}}</ref> Despite calls from dozens of local Democratic lawmakers to withdraw in favor of Bodnar, Alani Bankhead refused to do so.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Howard |first=Andrew |date=10 August, 2026 |title='I'll never bow down': Montana Democratic Senate nominee refuses to pave way for independent |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2026/08/10/montana-senate-bankhead-midterms-01031177 |url-status=live |access-date=2 November, 2026 |work=Politico}}</ref>
